  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I haven't run it in a browser or run `vite build`, so the rendering is unchecked. The scene is a ground plane plus exactly 10,000 instanced objects: 8,000 trunks (cylinders) and 8,000 canopies (cones), which make up the 8,000 trees, and 2,000 rocks (squashed spheres). That is 18,000 instances across 3 draws, since each tree's trunk and canopy are separate instances. A fixed-seed LCG places everything on a disc of radius 62, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours, and trunks share one brown. There is one directional light with shadows (4096 map, fitted to the forest) and exponential fog (`effects.fog` with mode \"exp\"). A hemisphere light and a neutral environment add fill. The camera orbits slowly at radius 88 and height 58, using `app.camera.setPose` each frame, and the whole forest is in view. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame is drawn. That flag fires two animation frames after the first `onFrame` callback, which assumes the engine draws that frame in between.",
